WEBVTT

00:08:29.116 --> 00:08:31.836
Maybe you want to speak to someone
in a different language

00:08:31.876 --> 00:08:34.676
and have that instantly translated
above the avatar's head.

00:08:34.716 --> 00:08:37.956
Perhaps you want to take your brainstorm
on top of Kilimanjaro

00:08:37.996 --> 00:08:40.316
or write your notes in dust on the Moon.

00:08:41.796 --> 00:08:46.316
And yet, with all of the amazing
possibilities afforded to us by VR,

00:08:47.396 --> 00:08:52.036
lots of our virtual environments
still mirror our physical environments.

00:08:52.076 --> 00:08:54.636
And there's a psychological
reason for this.

00:08:54.676 --> 00:08:56.956
A concept called “structured imagination”

00:08:56.996 --> 00:09:01.436
means that we tend to rely on existing
paradigms when we create things.